{"availability":"available","full":"proycon/colibri-core","name":"colibri-core","description":"Colibri core is an NLP tool as well as a C++ and Python library for working with basic linguistic constructions such as n-grams and skipgrams (i.e patterns with one or more gaps, either of fixed or dynamic size) in a quick and memory-efficient way. At the core is the tool ``colibri-patternmodeller`` whi      ch allows you to build, view, manipulate and query pattern models. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"C++","stars":135,"forks":20,"created":"2013-09-21T14:12:05Z","updated":"2026-02-05T12:15:41Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://proycon.github.io/colibri-core","topics":["c-plus-plus","computational-linguistics","corpus","library","linguistics","ngram","ngrams","nlp","pattern-recognition","python","skipgram","text-processing"],"demo":"https://proycon.github.io/colibri-core","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"curated-list","name":"Awesome Machine Learning","url":"https://github.com/josephmisiti/awesome-machine-learning"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z","stars":135,"forks":20}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["by Maarten van Gompel, proycon@anaproy.nl, Radboud University Nijmegen","Colibri Core is software to quickly and efficiently count and extract patterns from large corpus data, to extract various statistics on the extracted patterns, and to compute relations between the extracted patterns. The employed notion of pattern or construction encompasses the following categories:","N-gram extraction may seem fairly trivial at first, with a few lines in your favourite scripting language, you can move a simple sliding window of size n over your corpus and store the results in some kind of hashmap. This trivial approach however makes an unnecessarily high demand on memory resources, this often becomes prohibitive if unleashed on large corpora. Colibri Core tries to minimise these space requirements in several ways:"],"features":["n-gram -- n consecutive words","skipgram -- An abstract pattern of predetermined length with one or multiple gaps (of specific size).","flexgram -- An abstract pattern with one or more gaps of variable-size.","Compressed binary representation -- Each word type is assigned a numeric class, which is encoded in a compact binary format in which highly frequent classes take less space than less frequent classes. Colibri core…","Informed iterative counting -- Counting is performed more intelligently by iteratively processing the corpus in several passes and quickly discarding patterns that won't reach the desired occurrence threshold."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/proycon/colibri-core/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"a21a4eda58ad011a3979b6c28bcd87c08a15200f7ee5c510ade69e838d29920f","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"by Maarten van Gompel, proycon@anaproy.nl, Radboud University Nijmegen","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/proycon/colibri-core/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a21a4eda58ad011a3979b6c28bcd87c08a15200f7ee5c510ade69e838d29920f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/proycon/colibri-core/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-02-05T12:15:41Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/proycon/colibri-core/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T07:55:48.918Z","hash":"a21a4eda58ad011a3979b6c28bcd87c08a15200f7ee5c510ade69e838d29920f","originalBytes":7193,"storedBytes":7193,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["pattern","colibri","core","install","build","container","docker","colibri-core"